================================================================================
Mutable Instruments Plaits -- MIT
================================================================================

The MicroFreak's Speech engine is Mutable Instruments' Plaits LPC speech
synthesiser. This was established by byte-exact comparison against
`pichenettes/eurorack`, not by inference: the 14-byte frame struct, the
15-entry phoneme table, the quantisation lookup tables, the 640-entry
excitation pulse, and the word banks all match the published MIT source
value for value. The evidence is recorded in the companion
analysis repository, microfreak-emu.

Because that upstream source is MIT, the tables in this repository are
redistributable under the terms below. They are Emilie Gillet's work, not
Arturia's and not this project's.

The following files contain material derived from `pichenettes/eurorack`:

    microfreak/lpc.py
                       the energy, period and k0..k9 quantisation tables, and
                       the LPC bitstream layout, from
                       plaits/dsp/speech/lpc_speech_synth_controller.cc and
                       plaits/dsp/speech/lpc_speech_synth.h

    plugins/speech/mfreak_speech/render.py
                       a Python port of LPCSpeechSynth, and the 640-entry
                       int8 excitation pulse `lut_lpc_excitation_pulse`,
                       from plaits/dsp/speech/lpc_speech_synth.cc and
                       plaits/resources.cc

