================================================================================
Texas Instruments LPC10 speech data -- NOT redistributed
================================================================================

Plaits' five factory word banks are, in its own description, "LPC10-encoded
speech data extracted from Texas Instruments ROMs". The MicroFreak's banks
match them byte for byte.

This repository does not contain that data and must not come to contain it.
The tooling reads the banks out of a firmware image the user already owns,
at run time, and never writes them into source or into a committed artefact.
Keep it that way: the MIT licence covering the Plaits code around them is
not an obvious grant for speech recorded off a TI ROM, and nothing here
depends on redistributing it.


================================================================================
Arturia -- no code, no binaries, no affiliation
================================================================================

This project is not affiliated with, authorised by, endorsed by or connected
to Arturia in any way. "Arturia" and "MicroFreak" are trademarks of their
respective owners and are used here only to identify the hardware this
tooling was written for.

No Arturia code or data is included in this repository, and none should
ever be added to it. There are no firmware images, no bootloader dumps, no
factory vocabulary banks, no factory presets and no protocol captures here --
not gitignored copies of them, not samples of them, none. `.gitignore` refuses
`*.mff`, `*.raw` and `*.bin` as a second line of defence, but the first is that
every command takes the file it needs as an explicit argument.

Nothing is downloaded either. `fw patch` requires `--image`, pointing at a
payload you already own, and refuses any payload whose sha256 is not the one
its addresses were derived against.

Source comments and docstrings here describe observed behaviour and give
addresses within a firmware image. They do not reproduce it.
